UID:867dae9ca64cf254e60bcb426bb1dd7e@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: Arts & Crafts\\n\\nCome meet Field Museum 
 Artist in Residence Peggy Macnamara as she discusses her technique to seei
 ng - and sketching - the natural world. Visitors can try their hand at ske
 tching "unusual" specimens from Field Museum collections while learning mo
 re about Macnamara's five tips for sketching natural specimens: squint\, c
 rawl\, locate\, measure \, and correct . Peggy Macnamara has been the Fiel
 d Museum's Artist in Residence since 1990. She has traveled the world with
  Field Museum scientists to paint nature and illustrate conservation effor
 ts. She is also an Adjunct Professor at the School of the Art Institute of
  Chicago\, and is an exhibiting artist.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldm
 useum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/observational-drawing-using-unusual-
 specimens
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/observational-
 drawing-using-unusual-specimens
